WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
… and talk to them…
And the 30 others, which are coming,

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.080
should be day scholars.
Now these day scholars,

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.720
if they are there, should fund for this.
And the 10 Sahaja Yogis should fund it.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.040
So, it’s all right.
But out of these 30 day scholars,

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:21.531
if you find some children very good, etc.,
we can admit them for our school there.

00:00:21.531 --> 00:00:22.960
Yes. But, Shri Mataji…

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.624
So primary school should be started.
In every country, you can start.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:27.000
Yes, if we can, yes.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.200
So we can have creche.
Then we can have Montessori,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.240
and then we can have primary schools,
in every country.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.840
Out of those, when they pass out
from there,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.560
we’ll take them for our school there.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.400
In India, yes.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.240
In India.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.560
And Marie Martine has written a program
for primary school

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.720
based on Sahaja Yoga
and Montessori teaching.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.200
It is in French, but it is good. I have…

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.120
But for example, now the school
you are having there, in New York.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:57.600
It’s a creche.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.600
It’s kindergarten. You have nothing
of Sahaja Yoga there, nothing.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.280
I’m surprised, nothing of Sahaja Yoga.
You must teach them Sahaja Yoga.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.000
After all, you are not running
a Montessori.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.360
So in Montessori school-
come in, come in.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:11.440
Please come.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.320
What has been presented in this text
from Marie Martine

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.600
is that Anna Montessori has been
building a system

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.680
to wake up the inner quality
and spontaneity of the child.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.000
But this method is fulfilled by the
teaching of Shri Mataji Nirmala Devi

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.160
in Sahaja Yoga.
And that the Sahaja method of teaching

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:38.080
brings forward in its fullness
what Anna Montessori wanted to do.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:38.640
Yes.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.000
And so the accent is on the Sahaja
method of teaching

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.200
as introduced by Montessori,
and not the reverse as in Vienna.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.280
Because in Vienna
you are too ‘Montessorific’.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.080
Absolutely. I mean, I’m surprised
at the children also.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.600
They don’t know how to bow,
they don’t know how to say mantras…

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.085
Now, we’ll change this immediately,
Shri Mataji.

00:01:57.085 --> 00:01:59.400
You must change. You see,
best for that is this girl.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.200
What’s her name is, Sharminda.
She has been teaching

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.840
in a regular Sahaj school.
But ultimately, they’ll be coming

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.000
only to a Sahaj school.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.120
Because the way, you see, the way…

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.240
Montessori also,
you should keep up to a point.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.960
Yes, yes.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.160
Call it a Sahaj method.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.960
And you see, Marie-Martine has gone
in a Montessori school,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.600
and she could see extremely clearly
that what Anna Montessori wanted to do

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.160
is the spiritual transformation
of the child.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.040
But this is absolutely missing
in today’s Montessori schools,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.480
all over the place.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:32.920
Yes, of course.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.240
And we are the only one who can…

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.900
They become very materialistic.
Montessori children are

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.480
extremely materialistic.
They get attached to their toys

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.640
and things like that.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.840
But Shri Mataji, I am glad to hear it.
Because the way Warren presented it

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.320
a little bit sounded almost like
all children at the age of five

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.472
have all to go to Rome, which I feel,
I mean, of course I am biased…

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:53.480
Not all.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.040
Because I would like to spend at least
two or three years with my children

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.120
before they go to India.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.200
No, no, no, need not, need not.
Some should go to Rome, some…

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.760
wherever it is possible,
we should have schools everywhere,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.240
in every country. You see, they can have
children from Rome, around.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.480
And also visiting Sahaja Yogi,
but case by case, according to the need.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.000
Some people, like in England,
it’s rather difficult just now

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.760
to start a primary school.
Most of the English children

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.240
will have to go to Rome, no doubt.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.080
The system we have in Australia,
Shri Mataji,

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:27.080
is we have primary school in Melbourne.
But we’ve also applied

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:30.000
with the government
for government funding

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.240
to build and pay for the teachers
for a primary school

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.760
in Sydney and Perth in 1988.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:39.600
Teachers?

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.720
Sorry, the government will pay
for just about everything.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.320
For the primary? Yes, yes,
you can have it everywhere.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.680
Yes, that’s a very good idea,
very good idea.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.840
And this, then, once they are done,
then they can come here,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.640
and gradually we can make it
into a college and a university.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.520
This is it. And for Europe, I think,
in Europe,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.360
if one place would be built
above other places,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.880
it should probably be Rome.
But let’s have our primary school

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.320
as far as we can in the countries.
Let’s have one in France,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.480
let’s have one in Austria,
let’s have one in Switzerland.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.440
And in Rome, we can, we’ll have, anyway,
we’ll send children in Rome.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.320
But not on a systematic basis,
case by case.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.880
If children have to be separated
from their parents for any reason,

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:22.276
let them go.

00:04:22.276 --> 00:04:24.400
But in your case, they should be.
The way they are attached to you

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.840
is not good, Gregoire.
Both the children are suffering bodily.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.920
All the time, they’re slinging onto you.
They sit- their muscles are not good.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.160
Shri Mataji, they have never had
a proper family. Never.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.960
Whatever it is, but I think they should
be with the mother more than

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.920
with the thing.
Because they need massaging,

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.960
their muscles must grow
the way they hang on!

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.760
Especially Niranjana.
So much worried about her.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.560
Even Machindranath will go
and sit in his lap, you see.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.560
You see, he gets the heat
from other people.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.720
Children don’t grow well.
They should be independently playing.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.120
That’s very important.
I think this sticking on is too much.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.560
Shri Mataji, don’t you think
they stick on

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.200
because they are never with me?
They have a demand

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.520
for being in a family
for one or two years.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.040
Yes, that is maybe the reason.
But you see,

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.000
we should not add to their trouble.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.760
I don’t want that.
I don’t want that, Shri Mataji.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.320
But let us find out a solution.
And solution is that

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.040
more with the mother.
Say, Christine will be there.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.400
More with her.
Let her look after the children.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.680
I am not at all, Shri Mataji,
I don’t like to have children

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.600
long time with me.
I always send them away

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.080
after a few minutes.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.080
No, I understand them,
but this should not make it, you see,

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.520
a problem for them.
Because if their health goes down,

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.920
if their muscles go down, later on,
they will not develop their muscles.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.920
You see, this is the time
their muscles are to be grown.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.920
So it’s important that they should not
be all the time

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.320
on the body of a person.
Because you see, we emit heat

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.360
and their temperature
is different from ours.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.080
All those children, actually
one of the cases is like that.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.080
He’s spoiled, because the child –
who was that? Warren knows.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.320
Bhavani.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:59.360
Bhavani one, but another one,
whose health was very much ruined.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.800
I think two persons are there.
One is Olympia,

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.040
her muscles are not good.
There’s another child who has been

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.600
on the lap and lap, all the time.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.360
But this is easy
because if this is so, I can…

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.680
Because they are very light.
You lift the children,

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.040
they are very light, you see.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.000
But this is easy, Shri Mataji,
because this is the problem,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.840
I can just stop taking them on my lap.
But you see, I, my way,

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.400
I am mixing two things.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.360
No, no, not that way. You see,
they are used to it kind of thing.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.240
Now Christine is coming in,
she just can stop it.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.240
But she is to be told also
that you should see

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.920
that the children do not get
all the time clinging on to you,

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:41.000
taking this thing.
And that children should be independent

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.800
and should be massaged properly.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:49.600
Who is the child who was?…
I think, the children who have

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.800
very weak muscles is Olympia one,
another who is a very light child.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:59.800
Oh, it was his child,
the boy of Marcus.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.320
Amar.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:06.822
Marcus’ son. He is too very light.
It’s the same thing.

00:07:06.822 --> 00:07:06.834
It’s true.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.960
He is another child,
always taken in the lap.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.240
He is another child.
You see, you should be careful.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:15.520
Children should not be light.
You see, they must have weight.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.000
If they have weight,
then they can grow better.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.120
You see, this is very important.
If children are light

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.000
when you lift them…

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.440
Shakti is another one.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.440
Shakti is another one, very, very light.
She’s very light.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:27.360
Shakti is light?

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.880
No, I mean,
an example for heavy children.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:30.640
She is heavy?

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.800
Yes, she is very heavy.
She is enormous.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.240
In weight she is…

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.240
Siddhartha, for example, is light.
Siddhartha is too light.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:39.600
Your boys.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.040
Very light.
Siddhartha is very light also.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:47.000
I have not lifted Shakti so far,
so I don’t know.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.640
But could be a child looking fat,
could be very light.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:50.000
That’s true.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.240
Like I’ll tell you, Olympia is,
Olympia is very light.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.320
Even the child of Esther is very light.
Because Esther’s body, see,

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.240
she had very weak muscles
from childhood.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.600
But she was very pampered, she says.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.160
So whatever is good for them,
we should do it,

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:12.720
and it should not be a handicap
for them. It should be worked out.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.320
And this is another thing
worrying me a little bit,

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:19.320
that we must understand children
in totality, in a total way,

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:22.880
in a whole way, not in one partial way
or this way.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:28.360
And the only thing is,
we should achieve it.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:31.560
No explanation, nothing.
Just achieve it.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.840
Achieve good health for them.
It’s very important.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.520
The first thing we can give them
is good health. First thing.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:41.700
That’s very important.
That’s the primordial thing, is good.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.600
Then the second thing
would be good character.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.520
But the first thing is good health.
If the health is not good,

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.800
character can be also wrong, you see,
because health is not good.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:56.520
Mother, on the question of schools,
maybe I missed it out of the room,

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:00.880
but are we allowed to go ahead
with starting primary schools

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.720
in some of the major cities in Europe?
And say…

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:06.040
Let them start their own.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.720
America and Australia?

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.920
You see, let them start on their own.
Everyone can.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.555
Every country should take
the responsibility.

00:09:11.555 --> 00:09:13.440
So could Perth, for example,
start a school?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.320
Yes, yes, let them get it.
Anywhere, anywhere.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.192
Not all [unclear],
Perth, Sydney and Melbourne.

00:09:16.192 --> 00:09:17.440
Very good, very good.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.560
And we’ve got funding for all of those
coming up in 1988.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.880
If you look after them up to the age,
with a detached mind,

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:29.320
up to the age of, say, nine years,
it would be nice.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.080
But with a detachment,
that’s very important,

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:33.760
because you may spoil them completely.
When they come to India,

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:37.120
it may be very difficult for us.
That’s the time most important.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.080
It’s the formative time.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.280
Very formative. We cannot dare to have
children from younger age, you see,

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:45.280
because it’s rather risky.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.520
But what is the role of Rome, Mother,
in all this?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.400
Is there any special place for Rome?

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.880
No, nothing. Everybody should do.
But Rome has shown so well.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.640
I mean, they correct people very well.
Some children who are defective

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:59.080
are corrected by Rome, and all that.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.360
So, we could still go on like that.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.200
There will always be a surplus,
because we will not be able…

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.160
We have to be pragmatic.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.160
No, no, no.
It’s not a question of surplus or…

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.160
It’s not economics.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.080
No, I mean a surplus of children
for Rome. What I’m saying is…

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.240
No, no, no. Whether there are surplus
or not is not the point.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:18.960
But Rome has one advantage so far,
is that the children who have problems

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.680
are helped.
Like for among all the children,

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.080
Niranjana, I would say,
should go there, to Rome.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.880
Now, the report I have about Niranjana
is a little funny, but it is there,

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.760
that she’s a sly child. She’s sly.
She plays tricks, this, that,

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:38.280
and then tries to console the child.
It’s the report I’ve got for her.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.160
For such a child, they should go to Rome,
I personally think myself,

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.600
because they can be corrected.
Maybe she may not be corrected in, say…

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:49.880
we should be detached about it.
What is for their benevolence

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.160
we should do. For a while.
Till she’s corrected, she could be there,

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.560
because curriculum will be the same
everywhere.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.080
So they can be shifted
from this to there.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.480
We should be open about it,
because if a correction is needed,

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.120
a child should go there.
I would say, I was saying Shivani,

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:03.840
for example, this…

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:04.400
Bhavani.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.840
Bhavani. She should go to Rome.
A child like that.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.000
More sort of, because he knows
how to handle better.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:16.680
You see, they are little, little,
not very normal Sahaja Yogis,

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:20.720
little abnormal. Even your son
will be helped a lot, I would say.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:22.760
And probably even some from Australia.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:22.941
[Unclear] Shri Mataji.

00:11:22.941 --> 00:11:26.400
No, he will be very much helpful.
I agree, it is, it means

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:31.160
that you have to give your children.
But it’s like a child is sick now,

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.800
so you have to send him
to the hospital. It’s like that.

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:39.840
It’s very simple for us,
as long as you give us advice,

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.040
because you know everything.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:41.400
Yes.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.600
So this is, as far as,
if you tell Machidranath

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.340
has to go there, that’s…

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:47.240
Not all, not all. I would say
Machidranath is all right now,

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:51.280
I saw him and he’s all right.
But I would say, just Hugo’s child,

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.240
you see, the elder one,
younger one is all right.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.440
He still gets it. You see, they will
end up with schizophrenia,

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.680
must know that.
His habits, if it is continued,

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:00.720
they will end up in schizophrenia.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.720
This is very good,
keeping Rome as this purpose.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.400
So we have to be careful about children
who we see,

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:09.360
you have to be very careful.
If you see any symptom like that,

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.920
then try. And there’s no harm,
because it will be the same curriculum

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:13.300
he’ll be acting.

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:17.840
Yes, yes. This is perfectly…
we had two questions.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.560
One was to solve the system-wise,
and then there are

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.680
the case-by-case approach.
And I feel that

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.880
by the case-by-case approach,
if we are blessed

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:29.160
by your specific advice,
there is the list of the problem we know,

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:32.560
that’s the good for them.
But system-wise, I understand

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.680
it’s all right, that…

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:36.920
Shakti, I would say,
is an ideal Sahaja Yogini.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:38.920
Shakti, she is so good.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.600
Ideal Sahaja Yogini.
She doesn’t cry for help.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.680
She eats a lot, Shri Mataji.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.960
She’s an ideal Sahaja Yogini.
We can say Olympia is another one,

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:50.200
we can say.
But Olympia’s health is not all right.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.680
Her health is not all right,
because she eats very little,

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.880
she’s very light.
All these things are to be corrected,

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:57.480
no doubt about it.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:06.200
I saw her during the Havan,
but her attention was not there.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:06.800
Olympia?

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:10.520
Olympia. Not only, but she fell down.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.840
She had a bad accident outside
at the end of the puja.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:15.320
She always runs out
of all these programs,

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.200
also even now, she does it.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:21.280
And I think that’s a good reason
for her going to Rome just now, Mother.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.720
Niranjana, when I came to Rome…

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.080
I’ll see, unless the school starts,
just now, he is all right.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.800
But you must start a school,
then Warren, he can send him.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.320
We can’t afford to send them
to these public schools.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:33.320
Not permanently, OK.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:36.560
So, in that case,
another problem arises.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:44.840
We can have a school immediately there.
We can build a school in wood,

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:49.600
for instance. In two years, three years,
whenever we go away, we can dismantle.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:54.440
And that will cost probably
five, six thousand pounds.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.160
Oh, it’s all right.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:58.040
The problem is a problem of money
for Sahaja Yoga children,

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:02.240
that’s why we ought, for parents.
Because the alternative

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:06.480
is free school system.
So, for Sahaja Yoga parents,

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:11.000
I mean, I can work out just now
what I’m doing,

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.640
because I’m having no flat,
because I’m living in rooms

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.600
here and there.
If at some point I have to pay

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.920
for a flat, I cannot pay for Alison,
and school for my children,

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.120
and ashram in Rome. It’s too much.
I have not enough money for all this.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.600
No, but that’s one thing.
Another thing, Gregoire,

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:28.240
I would like to tell you,
that these problems need to be solved

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.120
on personal level. Now, let us do
one thing: what we can do,

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.160
we can start a school fund, separately.
These are personal things,

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.480
whether it’s yours, his or his.
It’s personal.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.000
It’s an example.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:41.520
Yes. But what I’m saying,
the attitude should be

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:45.240
that Sahaja Yogi should not be
liability on Sahaja Yoga.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:45.880
That’s it.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:49.680
By any chance. Should not expect
anything cheap or free also.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:53.640
Because once that you start…
I have gone through hell

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.520
with that kind of a thing.
Now, for a school, you have to pay.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:01.040
For example, if I start a school
in India, you are calculating

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:05.800
if you have to have the best school
with all music, dance, this, that,

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:09.160
horse riding, everything.
Has to be at least

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:12.280
per month hundred pounds.
Less than that won’t work out.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.920
This is perhaps fine with me,
Shri Mataji,

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.240
but many Sahaja Yogis
will not be able to afford this.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:22.480
Then those who cannot afford
should find something else.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.000
Because, you see, there will be
another school,

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.720
which will be a simpler school,
which will not work.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.360
Because who’s going to pay for it?

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.000
This is it.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:35.080
So what I’m saying, we will be able
to manage this school very well

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:41.240
in a way that, because I’ll expose it
to all the other countries also,

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:44.200
all kinds of people.
So it will be supported.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:47.960
But we have to keep some fees.
Some very brilliant students,

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.120
we might give them scholarship.
It’s different.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:53.080
But we cannot make it
a very free school.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:56.520
A hundred pounds per month is not much,
because that much you spend

00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:00.000
in any case in the Western countries.
Any school you send them.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.880
Even to an ordinary school you send it,
you spend so much.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:09.640
Shri Mataji, may I ask you a question?
Sometimes, for example,

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:13.040
now we are in the situation,
we are not in an ashram, but in a flat.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:17.120
So then if we are in a flat,
the child is only with the parents.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:21.680
Is it in the long run, something
which is negative in the way

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.040
that he is less with children?
Of course, he can be in the crèche,

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.680
he can meet other people
during the week.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:31.880
But still, because in the flat,
he is not so much with others,

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.280
is that maybe having a…

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:36.840
No, I mean, Sahaja Yogi
should live in ashrams.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.720
It’s a better idea, always.
It helps the children,

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:43.080
they become much more collective,
they get corrected, you see,

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:46.800
and a person must learn
to be collective. That’s very important.

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.000
I think that will help them.
In the West, especially,

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:52.720
it’s much better. Because Indians
are very collective by nature.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:56.720
You people are not, you see.
So, because the nature is such

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:58.440
around you,
you cannot be very collective.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:00.160
What’s it, Warren?

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.960
We were just thinking of this case
of Vijay. It really caused

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:08.240
a little problem that he said
that you gave him special permission

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.000
to move out of the ashram.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:10.520
Never.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.600
And all that sort of thing.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:12.760
Oh…

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.280
Mister [unclear].

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:18.160
But you see, when somebody says that,
you should verify with Me.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:18.880
We should, James.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.320
I just don’t like ringing Mother up
and saying…

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:21.920
No, but on such points you should.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:22.840
On such points, you should.
I never gave.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:22.920
He never meditates, Mother, never.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.800
He’s a hopeless case,
and now it’s a bad example

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:31.040
for everybody. It’s like an excuse.
The door’s a little bit open now,

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:33.840
and anybody who gets a little bit upset
at ashram life…

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.120
I mean, “Oh, look at Vijay.
Mother gave him permission

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:37.280
to move out of the ashram”.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:38.800
“Because he was so bad”, you tell them.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:43.800
You know, Mother, his wife now comes
to the centre every day,

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.080
just to be with the collective.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:45.920
That’s good. That’s an answer.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:50.680
Because she’s so fed up with sitting
in the shop- flat, just at home.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.960
Good, good. That’s a good thing.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.340
But he really is, has such a big ego.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:58.600
You see, he will be all right.
Let him pay for his flat quite a lot.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:17:59.160
He does.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.513
And let him become a …

00:18:00.513 --> 00:18:01.840
He was sent out because he was so bad.

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:03.440
He was so bad.
That’s what you should say.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:07.787
That’s the main reason
I might have said ‘yes’.

00:18:07.787 --> 00:18:13.080
Shri Mataji, the problem of financing
in Europe can be taken care if…

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:18.080
I mean, this, I do feel that nobody
should save money

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.080
on the back of Sahaja Yoga.
That’s why, for instance,

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:22.360
the girls who are working now
for our children,

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:25.960
they have to get some money.
And, for instance, the Swiss parents now,

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.480
they pay extra above the pension
for the children.

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:31.960
They pay something extra for the girls,
because there is labour there.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:35.280
And this should be so. In Europe,
we can solve this problem,

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:39.320
if we have some, as you had suggested,
if we have schools who absorb children

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:42.280
from the outside.
Then for, if there are parents

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.870
in Sahaja Yoga who cannot quite afford,
they can have a-

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.960
I can’t understand for primary school,
as long as you don’t have

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:51.720
all these extracurricular activities,
you should be able to manage

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:55.040
even with other students.
But even if you have other students,

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:58.200
it’s all right. It makes no difference.
But they should be day scholars.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.880
They should not be residents,
that’s one thing.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.120
Day scholar, yes.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.880
But you be very careful, Gregoire.
For money’s sake, you get them.

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:06.480
You should not get diseases and troubles
from them, you know.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:10.000
It can be very…
it’s a very dangerous idea.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.400
That’s the age of moulding.
And you see, you don’t know

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:16.720
what sort of families they come from.
You have to verify

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:20.440
if the parents are all right,
to find out what sort of parents

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:26.120
they are, if there’s been a divorce,
this, that, and the child, how he is,

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.120
how his vibrations are. Otherwise…

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:32.400
Actually, these international schools,
for example, we have one in Sydney,

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.080
becomes a dumping ground
for all the neurotic cases.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:39.520
It’s true. It’s true. I know that.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:44.760
Did you know, Shri Mataji,
the good private schools in Sydney

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:48.200
or in Australia, they say to you,
“Now, OK, you send your daughter

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:51.840
to our school, and if she misbehaves,
we will expel her. It’s up to you”.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:57.880
I mean, they just take no nonsense
at all. Because there’s a great fear

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:01.720
amongst parents in the West of,
shall we say, public schools.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:06.040
Very much, very much. And you see,
what is happening in Sahaja Yoga

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:09.560
is becoming like a liability
for all informs, all mads,

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:14.160
all this thing. That should be avoided.
It’s too much sometimes, it’s too much.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.160
We have to throw them out.
We cannot have such liabilities

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:17.640
upon ourselves.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:18.480
Yes.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:22.200
The way I think Marie-Martine would do,
she is going to get application.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.080
Then she’s going to see the parents,
talk with the parents,

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:29.520
explain Sahaja Yoga, say,
“This is Sahaja Yoga method.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.600
Do you agree with this?
There’ll be a meditation room,

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.840
this, that”.
And if they agree to this…

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.520
Then it’s all right.
But don’t worry about finances.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:37.160
It will work out.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:37.720
Yes, Shri Mataji.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.800
You see, we’ll get people.
But be careful on that,

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.520
“That we will expel your child
if he’s not behaving all right”.

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:45.960
This is important to say.
We don’t take liabilities.

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:48.720
Otherwise, all kinds of mad people
will be there.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:51.920
If you say we cure them,
we do nothing of the kind.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:56.000
We take very normal, good children,
well-behaved, of good families.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.360
Right. This is very important.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.480
This is very important.
I will tell Marie-Martine.

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:03.400
Don’t take all, otherwise
all kinds of mad people will be there.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.080
Yes, Shri Mataji.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:07.960
Only Sahaja Yogis’ children,
like her own child, can go to Rome.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:08.520
That’s it.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.320
She’s another possessed child,
do you know?

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.040
Sukanya?

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.080
Oh, Ma! She asked.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:13.960
She’s getting better, you know.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:19.520
Frequency, the frequency
of these attacks should lessen.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:24.360
I told already, I phoned already Rome
to find out the frequency.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:28.360
Frequency is very important.
If the frequency is less,

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:31.640
then it’s better. But otherwise,
there could be schizophrenia.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:39.240
Children, she is, she is about to.
You see, because when she was pregnant,

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:42.800
she used to still cry, weep,
do all kinds of things, I don’t know.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:46.200
And she was—the father especially
was thinking of the first child,

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:50.200
nonsense. He kept always her photograph
and all those things there.

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:54.640
Also, there was this pee-pee business.
Now she stopped.

00:21:54.640 --> 00:22:01.680
Because when she used to feel insecure
with someone, she just does pee-pee

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.440
in the bed or on the floor.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:04.040
Yes, everywhere.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:07.947
He’s getting such an expert,
Shri Mataji.

00:22:07.947 --> 00:22:10.520
Shri Mataji, it’s interesting to see
all the things come up to the surface,

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:15.960
because when Siddhartha is at home,
for example, he is very joyous

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:18.280
and living in.
As soon as he went to Rome,

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:21.600
because, I mean, he’s not
for the first two weeks now,

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:24.880
so it’s a change for him.
But he was very much residing

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:28.680
on the left-hand side.
And when we could see when Guru Puja,

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:31.680
he was meditating,
and attention was much better.

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:34.200
But still he was really much
on the left side.

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:38.575
So, it was sort of moving
from one side to another side.

00:22:38.575 --> 00:22:38.600
But still, it’s good…

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:40.960
So it’s good to face for the parents.

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:42.280
Yes. Hum?

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:45.560
It’s nice to teach him for the parents,
Shri Mataji.

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:47.720
Yes, but not all parents
are as sensible as you.

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:51.160
Yes, but you know, I mean, because…

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:55.000
Oh yes, yes, it’s true, no doubt.
Because they start criticizing.

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:59.520
They start criticizing.
This is the trouble.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:02.240
This is their liabilities.
They have everything free

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:06.480
and then criticize. Very nice.
Wonderful. See, Sahaja Yoga

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.600
should not be used as a liability.
That’s one thing, it’s very important.

00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:10.840
It’s getting too much for Me.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:12.320
Yes, Shri Mataji.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:18.240
Self-respect. Yes.
They lack self-respect.

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:22.220
They want to put all their problems
upon you, you solve it,

00:23:22.220 --> 00:23:25.880
and they think they should not spend
this, they have no money. Finished.

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:30.560
Why should we solve your problems?
In the West, it’s very much common.

00:23:30.560 --> 00:23:34.861
Not so much in the East.
In Maharashtra, let’s say

00:23:34.861 --> 00:23:36.200
in Maharashtra, we won’t have
these problems.

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:39.480
If I tell them, “You can’t afford,
we’ll have another kind of school”.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:40.960
They’ll say,
“All right, whatever we can afford”.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:45.880
One should be sensible about it,
it’s true.

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:49.680
But the idea of scholarship
is very good, Shri Mataji,

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:53.480
because we can say, “Okay, each child,
this is what is the mark”,

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:56.800
and if then there is an exception
to be made because somebody forces,

00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:58.080
then we can say
we give you a scholarship.

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:01.440
And also, we’ll, be, you see,
out of the gains of this school.

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:06.080
I’m thinking of starting another school,
somewhere else,

00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:09.760
a little away from Vaitarna,
somewhere else,

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:13.440
where it won’t be provided
with all these facilities,

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:17.040
that we’ll have here.
But it will be a good school

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:19.800
for Sahaja Yoga, where Indian boys
can go also,

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:23.360
and where these boys can also go,
those who cannot afford at all.

00:24:23.360 --> 00:24:29.040
We can get some children like that.
But this school cannot be maintained,

00:24:29.040 --> 00:24:33.400
I’ve found out, that if the kind of
ideas I have about the school,

00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:36.160
to equip them very well,
this thing cannot be maintained.

00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:39.760
Shri Mataji, we have to have the top,
because if I understand correctly,

00:24:39.760 --> 00:24:42.400
these people are supposed to be
the elite of the next generation.

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:46.520
Yes. And also, for those who cannot
afford, we can have scholarships.

00:24:46.520 --> 00:24:48.880
In every class, we can have three,
four good boys,

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.600
excellent boys have scholarships.
But they should not feel

00:24:51.600 --> 00:24:53.760
they are in scholarship.
They’ll also develop deficiencies.

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:56.800
That would be secret. That would be
between the administration

00:24:56.800 --> 00:24:59.720
and the parents. Nobody would know
who has a scholarship, who does not.

00:24:59.720 --> 00:25:00.440
Yes.

00:25:00.440 --> 00:25:03.160
Shri Mataji, I often tell the parents
in Australia,

00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:07.400
if you can’t afford the fees,
get a better job. Get a better job.

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:11.160
Must. To earn more money.
If you can’t afford the fees,

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:12.120
get a better job.

00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:13.960
Yes, they should work it out.

00:25:13.960 --> 00:25:15.320
We should have that attitude.

00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:20.520
Yes, any such problem, we should say,
“This is your problem, finished.

00:25:20.520 --> 00:25:24.920
Yes, you can get two jobs, the father,
if he has to,

00:25:24.920 --> 00:25:27.360
because to educate the child
that he’s been blessed with.

00:25:28.160 --> 00:25:30.920
Both of them can work.
The mother and father both.

00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:32.240
Don’t try that in England.

00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:38.080
This is what I’m a little bit
worried about. Because, yes, yes.

00:25:38.080 --> 00:25:40.400
Because at that time, Shri Mataji,
you mentioned that the English

00:25:40.400 --> 00:25:43.320
Sahaja Yogis would never be able
to pay in Rome.

00:25:43.320 --> 00:25:46.160
And that’s where my worries started,
I should say.

00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:50.320
Yes, in Rome they can pay
up to the primary school.

00:25:50.320 --> 00:25:53.080
But you see, in England, if you have
to send any child to a school,

00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:58.680
the fees and all that, and the food
and everything, and conveyors,

00:25:58.680 --> 00:26:03.240
clothes, and all, this thing will be
about a hundred pounds per child,

00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:03.880
isn’t it?

00:26:04.920 --> 00:26:06.360
Not in a private school.

00:26:06.360 --> 00:26:06.960
Hum?

00:26:06.960 --> 00:26:08.160
Private school but…

00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:12.480
No, no, no, no. Even in other schools.
In ordinary schools…

00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:14.020
Ordinary schools,
there’s no fees for school.

00:26:14.020 --> 00:26:14.160
No fees.

00:26:15.680 --> 00:26:17.400
Obviously looking after the child…

00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:17.840
Yes.

00:26:17.840 --> 00:26:19.320
It costs you money.

00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:24.640
No fees in the primary school.
But they have no facilities.

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:26.800
Just go to school, come back,
that’s all.

00:26:26.800 --> 00:26:30.920
You see, so, I mean,
for a private school,

00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:33.080
it’s more than two hundred.

00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:34.280
That’s why, yes.

00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:35.680
So this is in between, you see.

00:26:36.520 --> 00:26:37.320
Yes, that’s why.

00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:44.320
I mean, hundred pounds is, I think,
they’ll have to work harder for that,

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:49.120
for their children, isn’t it?
But we can’t do it for fifty pounds,

00:26:49.120 --> 00:26:49.960
can we?

00:26:49.960 --> 00:26:51.540
No, you should not, Shri Mataji…

00:26:51.540 --> 00:26:53.360
We shouldn’t skint
on the money at all.

00:26:53.360 --> 00:26:58.520
No, but, I mean, there should be
a setting in which people

00:26:58.520 --> 00:27:00.600
who are running this school
are not embarrassed.

00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:01.720
I mean, they should have…

00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:04.960
Or else we can charge a percentage
on the earnings of the parents.

00:27:04.960 --> 00:27:12.840
No, no, no. That’s forbidden.
Everybody will then downgrade

00:27:12.840 --> 00:27:16.600
their jobs.
Just to get onto the bandwagon.

00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:18.680
They’ll all go on the dole.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:22.480
Or else we can do one more thing:
in low classes,

00:27:22.480 --> 00:27:26.480
we can charge a little less.
In the higher classes, little higher.

00:27:26.480 --> 00:27:28.960
It’s perhaps better, Shri Mataji,
to have one price

00:27:28.960 --> 00:27:31.760
which you say is a hundred pounds.
And then, case by case,

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:35.720
give some partial scholarship
for people who say, “I just can’t”.

00:27:35.720 --> 00:27:39.640
For instance, if someone has one child,
okay, if someone has more children…

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:43.520
I’m not thinking about me,
I know what is the suspicion.

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:44.760
Five [unclear] three.

00:27:44.760 --> 00:27:45.040
Me too, me too…

00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:51.240
You see, I have four grandchildren
and C.P. would be retired.

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:55.000
If I have to put my grandchildren
there. You see, think of it.

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.280
He’ll be retired man.

00:27:57.320 --> 00:28:01.650
Well, I’m not going into this
discussion, Shri Mataji.

00:28:01.650 --> 00:28:04.280
But not thinking about myself,
I’m sure.

00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:06.680
And then have a guy buying a car
which will run on petrol.

00:28:06.680 --> 00:28:09.120
Ah, car, Mother.
India’s just burned up.

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:09.600
Hum?

00:28:09.600 --> 00:28:13.920
The car fever is on.
The car fever is on, here and there.

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:14.280
Where?

00:28:16.240 --> 00:28:18.920
Djamel has bought you a car.

00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:19.200
Hum?

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:23.440
He’s put a down payment,
it’s not fixed by any means,

00:28:23.440 --> 00:28:26.960
on a big new Contessa
with a Japanese engine

00:28:26.960 --> 00:28:28.640
and air conditioning and everything.

00:28:29.840 --> 00:28:33.040
Where? In India? Djamel?

00:28:33.040 --> 00:28:35.840
India? How Djamel can put?

00:28:35.840 --> 00:28:40.280
Not Djamel. Jalan, Jalan.

00:28:40.280 --> 00:28:43.760
That they are going to buy,
not from my, from their own money.

00:28:45.120 --> 00:28:46.960
That they are going to buy one for Me.

00:28:47.480 --> 00:28:50.240
But this is normal, because you need
one in Maharashtra

00:28:50.240 --> 00:28:54.120
and you need one in Bihar.
When you go to Calcutta.

00:28:54.120 --> 00:28:57.760
I’m not going to Bihar. But you see,
this car, that one…

00:28:57.760 --> 00:29:00.008
I think you should have it, Mother.

00:29:00.008 --> 00:29:00.012
Hum?

00:29:00.012 --> 00:29:00.031
You should have it.

00:29:00.031 --> 00:29:00.040
Two cars.

00:29:00.040 --> 00:29:02.520
Because for two or three years,
you’re not having a car.

00:29:02.520 --> 00:29:05.000
You see, what happens, suppose
in one car fails, then another,

00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:07.960
at least two cars should move out.
It’s all right, we can have.

00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:11.440
This car they are buying
from the trust.

00:29:12.800 --> 00:29:14.640
They’ve done it.
They’ve put a deposit down.

00:29:15.320 --> 00:29:17.060
How much it is?

00:29:17.060 --> 00:29:20.040
Fifteen thousand.
He’s already got one himself.

00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:23.600
He wants one for you.
And they’re working it out.

00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:26.320
So, I think next tour, Mother,
you’ll have a Contessa.

00:29:28.680 --> 00:29:29.560
Wonderful.

00:29:29.560 --> 00:29:31.960
My God, at least some comfort.

00:29:31.960 --> 00:29:34.720
So, the car fever is on,
there and here.

00:29:34.720 --> 00:29:36.720
What is the Contessa?
What is a Contessa?

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.360
Yes, yes, for four years I’ll have
no car in any case.

00:29:41.360 --> 00:29:45.680
Just think of it. Till this car goes,
I’ll have no car there.

00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:48.320
So, I need something for four years,
I can use Contessa.

00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:53.960
There’s no car,
that Duma’s car has to go.

00:29:53.960 --> 00:29:56.160
We’ll have to buy one in Australia
for you, Mother.

00:29:56.160 --> 00:29:58.480
You should have, Shri Mataji,
I really feel you should have

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:00.960
a Mercedes for India.
Not one of these things.

00:30:00.960 --> 00:30:02.440
No, no, but we can’t take just now.

00:30:02.440 --> 00:30:03.800
Just now, just now. Four years.

00:30:03.800 --> 00:30:05.280
I know, I understood that.

00:30:05.280 --> 00:30:07.320
It is for four years, what will I do?

00:30:07.320 --> 00:30:08.880
Are you still four years in Europe?

00:30:08.880 --> 00:30:10.520
At least three and a half years.

00:30:10.520 --> 00:30:13.960
No, but in two and a half, actually,
she’ll transfer her things,

00:30:13.960 --> 00:30:14.800
then come back.

00:30:15.800 --> 00:30:17.120
And then the car has to spare…

00:30:17.120 --> 00:30:20.720
Then transfer of residence
will be in three and a half years, yes.

00:30:21.440 --> 00:30:22.040
That’s it.

00:30:24.280 --> 00:30:25.440
So, Shri Mataji.

00:30:27.160 --> 00:30:29.720
I’ll have some car at least there,
Contessa.

00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:30.000
[Unclear].

00:30:30.960 --> 00:30:34.840
Then when she takes her car to India,
this station wagon [SW],

00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:37.040
we then have to buy her a car
for here.

00:30:37.040 --> 00:30:37.840
That will be.

00:30:37.840 --> 00:30:40.520
And when you come in the United States,
you’ll have a Cadillac.

00:30:40.520 --> 00:30:42.120
A Cadillac.

00:30:42.120 --> 00:30:42.720
Yours.

00:30:42.720 --> 00:30:43.680
Lincoln, Lincoln.

00:30:43.680 --> 00:30:44.880
I think better have Lincoln.

00:30:44.880 --> 00:30:47.800
Lincoln? Jai Shri Mataji!

00:30:47.800 --> 00:30:50.480
For heaven’s sake,
don’t spoil my name there.

00:30:51.680 --> 00:30:56.760
Have something normal.
Otherwise, they’ll count Me

00:30:56.760 --> 00:30:58.720
like other gurus, this, that.

00:30:58.720 --> 00:30:58.760
Never.

00:30:58.760 --> 00:31:01.400
No, but it should be comfortable
like Me.

00:31:01.400 --> 00:31:02.720
Shri Mataji, after all, you see.

00:31:03.520 --> 00:31:04.360
Why shouldn’t they buy?

00:31:04.360 --> 00:31:07.160
What is the… Rajabai at some point
said Shri Mataji should not have

00:31:07.160 --> 00:31:10.280
a Mercedes in India because then
the people think she gets money

00:31:10.280 --> 00:31:13.520
from others. The hell!
Why shouldn’t you have a Mercedes?

00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:16.640
Not Rajabai, he may not say that,
but somebody must say that.

00:31:16.640 --> 00:31:17.460
Let them go to….

00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:22.040
Rajabai is the one who will buy,
if you leave it to him,

00:31:22.040 --> 00:31:24.240
he’ll buy Lincoln for Me.
So, what do I care?”

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:25.600
But that’s correct.

00:31:25.600 --> 00:31:28.120
But not Me. You can say that.
It’s all right after all.

00:31:28.120 --> 00:31:28.760
So we do.

00:31:29.760 --> 00:31:31.347
Now where is this man?
He is not coming still.

00:31:31.347 --> 00:31:34.840
He’s not coming,
our collective desire to sit here.

00:31:34.840 --> 00:31:40.880
No, no, but I have to go.
We have to see that electrical stuff.

00:31:40.880 --> 00:31:42.760
Oh, Francis too.

00:31:42.760 --> 00:31:46.560
Just work out. Just work out
and see to that.

00:31:46.560 --> 00:31:49.960
You’ve seen the shop, reliable?
You know the shop better.

00:31:49.960 --> 00:31:51.520
Which one? Electrical?

00:31:51.520 --> 00:31:53.440
Around the station,
there are several shops.

00:31:53.960 --> 00:31:56.560
But it’s not a very nice area,
I must say.

00:31:57.600 --> 00:32:02.040
We should take mother to Promart then.
Or something like that, one big place.

00:32:02.040 --> 00:32:02.920
Do you know that place?

00:32:02.920 --> 00:32:03.200
No.

00:32:04.240 --> 00:32:09.960
We had bought once, you remember,
from one shop. That one was very good,

00:32:09.960 --> 00:32:12.080
but there are many, many things
like that.

00:32:12.080 --> 00:32:14.480
Oh, that place, we can go there,
Shri Mataji, ‘Hurti’.

00:32:15.080 --> 00:32:17.160
The one you went to last time
and bought the bowls.

00:32:17.160 --> 00:32:17.280
Yes.

00:32:17.280 --> 00:32:18.120
Yes, we can go there.

00:32:20.720 --> 00:32:21.640
This person…

00:32:22.280 --> 00:32:24.480
Don’t forget, Shri Mataji,
this gentleman will be here…

00:32:24.480 --> 00:32:25.760
by what time?

00:32:25.760 --> 00:32:26.400
Between 2 and 3.

00:32:26.400 --> 00:32:28.040
He was coming at 11.30 last time.

00:32:28.040 --> 00:32:30.600
No, no, 2 and 3 for the car,
the Mercedes.

00:32:31.280 --> 00:32:32.400
Well, 3 I’ll be back.

00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:32.800
Yes.

00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:35.520
He said he wanted to ring up
when he leaves.

00:32:36.480 --> 00:32:36.960
Right.

00:32:36.960 --> 00:32:37.520
For…

00:32:37.520 --> 00:32:37.960
Shri Mataji.

00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:38.960
Oh, sorry.

00:32:38.960 --> 00:32:42.200
Shri Mataji, my apologizes
if I interrupt you,

00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:45.600
because you talked to Guido
about Siddhartha

00:32:45.600 --> 00:32:49.520
and you wanted to give me
one or two advices, I think, about…

00:32:52.640 --> 00:32:57.360
I’ve forgotten what I wanted to tell you
about, but I think it over.

00:33:03.800 --> 00:33:07.000
You see, Siddhartha has that
Venezuelan problem on him.

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.400
Yes, I have the feeling
from his birth, that’s it.

00:33:16.360 --> 00:33:22.600
Poor children. Bhoots are one
of the horrible things.

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:24.800
And one thing I’ve seen,
if you move children

00:33:24.800 --> 00:33:28.320
from their own place,
bhoots leave them quite a lot.

00:33:31.560 --> 00:33:33.080
You see, they belong to a place.&nbsp;

00:33:39.800 --> 00:33:41.120
They don’t go very far, yes.

00:33:47.440 --> 00:33:51.120
They will be staying with us
until when?

00:33:51.120 --> 00:33:55.360
If it is possible, maybe till
it is going better,

00:33:55.360 --> 00:33:57.960
then maybe, can come back
for the Krishna puja.

00:33:57.960 --> 00:33:59.320
Or something, let us see.

00:34:00.280 --> 00:34:02.200
Shri Mataji, as far…

00:34:02.200 --> 00:34:05.560
Frequency should be seen.
Frequency is the only way

00:34:05.560 --> 00:34:08.560
we can determine
if they are improving or far.

00:34:08.560 --> 00:34:10.480
It should not appear
for at least six months,

00:34:10.480 --> 00:34:14.320
then, then it’s all right.
Because, you see, the parents,

00:34:14.320 --> 00:34:15.920
when they see, they become sort of…

00:34:15.920 --> 00:34:17.945
It means the end of the year, Mother.

00:34:17.945 --> 00:34:18.800
End of the year. Yes.

00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:19.200
Let it be. Let it be.

00:34:19.200 --> 00:34:22.440
And also, Shri Mataji, the way I’ve
understood things is that

00:34:22.440 --> 00:34:27.360
my children would stay in Rome.
They are in Rome since one year or so,

00:34:27.360 --> 00:34:28.520
no? No?

00:34:28.520 --> 00:34:31.340
They came in October.

00:34:31.340 --> 00:34:34.720
In October last year.
So, the way I understand things

00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:36.600
is that they would stay in Rome…

00:34:36.600 --> 00:34:37.360
Otherwise what?

00:34:37.360 --> 00:34:39.360
At least till the end of the year.

00:34:39.360 --> 00:34:40.560
Otherwise, what is the solution?

00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:43.400
Till the end of the year.

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:44.960
Otherwise what is the solution?

00:34:44.960 --> 00:34:51.440
Otherwise, I have, on this basis,
because I am not…

00:34:52.720 --> 00:34:54.720
There are two possibilities.
May I answer your question,

00:34:54.720 --> 00:34:56.560
Shri Mataji? If I get this job…

00:34:56.560 --> 00:35:00.740
That’s it. So, you see what I’m saying,
you yourself are in a transition,

00:35:00.740 --> 00:35:01.160
Gregoire.

00:35:01.160 --> 00:35:02.573
That’s it. That’s why I…

00:35:02.573 --> 00:35:04.240
So, it’s a much more suitable thing
that way.

00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:06.200
For me, it is ideal
if they can stay until…

00:35:06.200 --> 00:35:06.920
It is ideal. Yes.

00:35:06.920 --> 00:35:08.560
For me, it is ideal
if they can stay until…

00:35:08.560 --> 00:35:10.880
That’s what I asked you,
what is the otherwise?

00:35:10.880 --> 00:35:13.400
Because nothing is better,
so much better than this.

00:35:13.400 --> 00:35:14.040
Let them be there.

00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:19.680
If by any chance that US business
does not work, then what would happen,

00:35:19.680 --> 00:35:24.040
probably, is that Ruth and Kingsley
have just arrived,

00:35:24.040 --> 00:35:27.320
and they are transitory too
for three months.

00:35:27.320 --> 00:35:29.000
Then if I don’t get this job
within three months,

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:30.960
then we can take… start an ashram.

00:35:30.960 --> 00:35:31.840
That you can see later on.

00:35:31.840 --> 00:35:32.840
Later on.

00:35:32.840 --> 00:35:34.760
But what I’m saying, just now
I have a feeling,

00:35:34.760 --> 00:35:39.840
if you get a job in America,
under such transition conditions…

00:35:39.840 --> 00:35:42.160
I mean, we, when we were transferred
and all that,

00:35:42.160 --> 00:35:44.200
we used to leave our children
with parents.

00:35:44.200 --> 00:35:47.600
And because we had to arrange
our transfer, go there, take over,

00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:48.640
lots of problems are there.

00:35:48.640 --> 00:35:52.560
Yes, that absolutely.
Later and afterwards we can see…

00:35:52.560 --> 00:35:54.360
Once you are settled down.
Don’t take children

00:35:54.360 --> 00:35:55.280
in unsettled conditions.

00:35:55.280 --> 00:35:56.440
Yes, Shri Mataji.

00:35:56.440 --> 00:35:58.480
Where they are settled down is better,
they are settled down.

00:35:58.480 --> 00:36:00.320
They are accepted there,
they are there.

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:04.160
I registered Machindranath at a school,
in Rome, until December.

00:36:04.160 --> 00:36:08.400
Yes, it’s all right, let him be there.
You see, it is more to keep them

00:36:08.400 --> 00:36:11.160
settled than anything else.
Than to take them

00:36:11.160 --> 00:36:14.720
in the nomadic conditions
when you are moving

00:36:14.720 --> 00:36:19.000
from one place to another.
That upsets children very much.

00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:20.600
The food, the timing, everything.

00:36:22.120 --> 00:36:26.720
One last question, Shri Mataji.
I’ve said to the parents, sorry,

00:36:26.720 --> 00:36:29.840
that the mothers who didn’t go
on Indian tour last year,

00:36:29.840 --> 00:36:35.000
should all go this year
and we start a creche just while the…

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.000
Is that acceptable?

00:36:36.600 --> 00:36:39.120
Yes, that’s all right.
If there is somebody to look after

00:36:39.120 --> 00:36:39.920
the children. It’s sensible.

00:36:39.920 --> 00:36:41.200
Oh yes, we have many mothers there.

00:36:41.200 --> 00:36:43.760
There’s no harm.
You can run the creche nicely.

00:36:43.760 --> 00:36:46.320
The mothers could come.
And also I was thinking,

00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:50.280
children about, say, ten years or so,
we can bring them to India.

00:36:50.280 --> 00:36:52.520
No harm, because in any case
they have to come to India.

00:36:53.520 --> 00:36:54.836
About nine years or ten years.

00:36:54.836 --> 00:36:57.120
That would be a wonderful experience,
some on Indian tour.

00:36:57.120 --> 00:36:59.440
Children should come,
because they have to come to India

00:36:59.440 --> 00:37:04.040
at that age, later on.
Ten years is all right.

00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:07.040
So my wife, Diane, Mother,
she wants to come on Indian tour.

00:37:07.040 --> 00:37:07.740
Is that okay?

00:37:07.740 --> 00:37:08.440
Let her come. Yes, very important.

00:37:13.880 --> 00:37:16.880
Thank you.

00:37:16.880 --> 00:37:19.840
And children should be in a creche.
Those who can afford it,

00:37:19.840 --> 00:37:21.840
you should put them in a creche
or something.

00:37:24.720 --> 00:37:26.840
But, Gregoire, in Sahaja Yoga,
you see, manage things

00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:33.200
at a minimum price than anything else.
I tell you, if I have to educate

00:37:33.200 --> 00:37:36.760
my own grandchildren in England,
it would cost Me such a lot!

00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:40.080
Yes. There is no doubt about this.

00:37:40.080 --> 00:37:42.280
Even in India, say,
dual school and all that.

00:37:43.080 --> 00:37:47.560
Oh, oh, oh, the amount they charge!
It comes to much more than, I mean,

00:37:47.560 --> 00:37:51.640
150 pounds per month.
Dual school is very expensive.

00:37:52.520 --> 00:37:54.280
And what is the education?
Nothing special.

00:37:54.280 --> 00:37:57.280
What is the school? Nothing.
Another has gone down like this,

00:37:57.280 --> 00:37:59.000
thinned down, blackened to such.

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:04.560
Can I have one more pair, I think.
Is it warm now enough?

00:38:04.560 --> 00:38:05.080
Yes.

00:38:05.080 --> 00:38:07.640
Then I’ll just now go walking.
Let’s walk out of that place.

00:38:07.640 --> 00:38:09.600
It’s a beautiful day. Beautiful.

00:38:11.360 --> 00:38:15.000
Everybody will think that you have
bodyguard, Shri Mataji,

00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:16.400
if we all walk around you like this.

00:38:16.400 --> 00:38:17.520
That’s good. Yes.

00:38:18.040 --> 00:38:19.120
All right, I’ll have my shoes.

00:38:19.800 --> 00:38:21.840
This lady said we’re looking
like a football team.

